Z||000010||StuGood||03-22-2001||07:13 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by warkior:<BR><B>...I heard from one individual that to change the plugs one must drop the engine...  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Let me guess...  this particular individual is an expert on practically everything, has worked on "lots of cars," and one time blew an engine in the middle of a desert, but had a pocket knife, so rebuilt the motor, etc., etc. ?<P>No, you definitely do <B>not</B> have to drop the engine to change plugs in a Fiero.  Unless you just want to make more work for yourself   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 03-22-2001).]||||reg||13
